  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Oblonganoside C may interact with Serine/threonine-protein kinase PLK4 through multiple indirect pathways. Path_44034 links Oblonganoside C to K-252a, which in turn targets PLK4, while Path_44035 connects Oblonganoside C to SBK1, which is also targeted by Theasaponin E1, another compound that ultimately affects PLK4. Path_44036 indicates that Oblonganoside C may interact with a tyrosine-protein kinase, which is targeted by a complex compound, and this complex also affects PLK4. These findings collectively suggest that Oblonganoside C may influence PLK4 through a series of downstream targets, possibly via the activation or inhibition of upstream kinases. The strength of the evidence is moderate, with scores ranging from 0.591 to 0.6255, indicating some level of confidence in the observed relationships. The mechanisms involve kinase-targeting pathways, suggesting a potential role for Oblonganoside C in modulating PLK4 activity, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm these interactions.",
